From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: Raise the A750 autosuspend delay to 200 ms

On A750 (SM8650), a runtime suspend that starts shortly after a resume
spins for the full ADRENO_IDLE_TIMEOUT in a6xx_gmu_wait_for_idle() and
then falls back to a6xx_gmu_force_off(). spin_until() busy-waits, so
each such suspend burns one second of CPU in the pm workqueue.

With the default 66 ms inactive_period, a bursty UI (a few short GPU
wakeups per second) hits this on about every other suspend. In the
slow case a7xx_gmu_gx_is_on() is never reached, i.e. the GMU never
reports the IFPC power state: it is the GMU that does not idle, not
GX that stays up. On a7xx the driver does not program the IFPC
hysteresis, so the GMU firmware's own (gen70900, v4.2.20) is in play.

Measured on an AYANEO Pocket S2 (SM8650), 7.2.9, idle UI, 60 s
windows, GPU runtime suspends that took > 100 ms:

  autosuspend_delay_ms   slow suspends   kworker CPU
  66 (default)           8 of 16         18%
  100                    9 of 19         -
  200                    0 of 9          6%
  500                    0 of 7          7%

Every slow suspend began 70-85 ms after the preceding resume; every
suspend after the GPU had been up for ~4 s completed in ~1 ms. The
same image on an A740 (SM8550, IFPC enabled, GMU v4.1.9) completed
52 of 52 suspends in <= 1.5 ms at 66 ms.

Use 200 ms for A750, the smallest tested value with no slow suspend.
A5xx entries already set a per-GPU 250 ms.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
novadeck: not posted. Workaround for the trigger, not the GMU root cause.
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -1588,7 +1588,7 @@
 			[ADRENO_FW_GMU] = "gmu_gen70900.bin",
 		},
 		.gmem = 3 * SZ_1M,
-		.inactive_period = DRM_MSM_INACTIVE_PERIOD,
+		.inactive_period = 200,
 		.quirks = ADRENO_QUIRK_HAS_CACHED_COHERENT |
 			  ADRENO_QUIRK_HAS_HW_APRIV |
 			  ADRENO_QUIRK_PREEMPTION |
